+# Aegis Autonomy Mode Runbook
+
+Purpose
+- Define and operate autonomy modes (OFF, SANDBOX, HYBRID, AUTONOMOUS).
+- Provide safe flip/runbook, monitoring, rollback and audit steps.
+
+Modes (brief)
+- OFF: No agent tool calls; agents can only suggest proposals (read‑only).
+- SANDBOX: Agents may call low‑risk tools in isolated sandboxes; no infra/actuation.
+- HYBRID: Agents may call medium‑risk tools with automated approvals for predefined plans and human approvals for high‑risk steps.
+- AUTONOMOUS: Pre‑approved flows only; reserved for vetted internal workloads; strictly monitored and auditable.
+
+Preconditions to flip a mode
+1. OPA policy loaded and validated (ops/policy/opa_autonomy.rego).
+2. Capability catalog populated (ops/policy/autonomy_tool_catalog.yaml).
+3. Evidence signer (cosign) and Rekor connectivity validated.
+4. Monitoring dashboards deployed (Grafana panels for safety, audit, and cost).
+5. Approver / multisig service available and healthy.
+6. Canary namespace and tests green for 72 hours.
+
+How to flip modes (cluster list/command examples)
+1. Update AutonomyMode CR (k8s/autonomy/autonomy-mode-cr.yaml) for target namespace.
+2. Verify OPA PDP receives new mode (query OPA endpoint).
+3. Run canary flows in SANDBOX for 24–72h (see tests in ops/ci/autonomy_tests.yml).
+4. Inspect evidence bundles in artifact store and Rekor entries.
+5. If metrics (blocked_calls, safety_violations) are acceptable, proceed to HYBRID with limited agent groups.
+
+Rollback procedure
+1. Set AutonomyMode CR to previous (e.g., OFF).
+2. Revoke any active agent tokens (rotate SA / ephemeral credentials).
+3. Trigger orchestrator to terminate running agent jobs (or scale to 0).
+4. Run incident collection: pull evidence bundles for affected runs and attach to incident ticket.
+
+Key Prometheus alerts to watch during flip
+- aegis_agent_safety_violations_total > 0 (page)
+- aegis_blocked_tool_calls_total spikes (warning)
+- retrain_guard_denies_total increases (warning)
+- QPU queue cost > threshold (warning)
+
+Acceptance criteria for mode promotion
+- Automated tests pass (autonomy tests, red‑team scenarios).
+- No safety violations in canary windows.
+- Auditable evidence exists for each tool invocation.
+- Multisig approvals recorded for any high‑risk action executed.
+
+Notes
+- Always ensure COSIGN KMS keys and Rekor are available before promoting any mode that allows signed promotions.
+- Keep a short human approval window when moving to HYBRID/AUTONOMOUS.
+
